  "note": "Room themes (October 5, draft for founder review; drawn only with the look panel's Room themes toggle on). A themed room's practical lights (lanterns, wall and standing torches) lean toward practical by practicalPull (and burn at practicalValue of their brightness, 1 when absent), its cold glows toward cold by coldPull. A plain hall keeps its skin's colours. Those tints stay inside the existing light classes: warm hue 15-50 with saturation at least 0.3, cold hue 160-270 with saturation at least 0.2. Each themed room also gets one accentLight, and its accent props (brazier flames, the dead fire's embers and their floor pools) burn in glow (or, for an accent pool, the accent light's own colour); both belong to the room-accent class below when glowClass is accent (RoomThemeAccents.Validate, the room themes proof).",
